        "original_id": "addfa938-3eaf-59fd-b6c9-e8538526a004",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lee Ranaldo, Mary Ramsey, Robert Buck, John Lombardo\n- Bands and Music Projects: Sonic Youth, 10,000 Maniacs, John & Mary, Between the Times and the Tides, Triangles\n- Companies: Matador Records\n- Places: Buffalo, New York\n- Roles: musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, record producer, lead singer, violinist\n\nFacts:\n- Lee Ranaldo was born on February 3, 1956.\n- Lee Ranaldo is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of the alternative rock band Sonic Youth.\n- Mary Ramsey was born on December 24, 1963.\n- Mary Ramsey is a resident of Buffalo, New York.\n- Mary Ramsey is a member of the folk rock duo John & Mary and the lead singer and violinist for the American alternative rock band 10,000 Maniacs.\n- Robert Buck, the lead guitarist of 10,000 Maniacs, died in 2000.\n- John Lombardo left 10,000 Maniacs for the second time in 2003.\n- Between the Times and the Tides is the ninth studio album by Lee Ranaldo.\n- Between the Times and the Tides was released on March 20, 2012, by Matador Records.\n- Triangles was the first 10,000 Maniacs release of new material since Robert Buck's death in 2000.\n- Triangles was the first 10,000 Maniacs album featuring singer Mary Ramsey without her songwriting partner John Lombardo after his 2003 departure.",
